// The VSCodium build the PartCAD IDE is made from.
//
// `version` is a VSCodium release tag (`1.106.1.25293`, say). Leave it `null` to
// build from whatever VSCodium released last, which is what an unattended build
// does today; set it to a tag to pin, and the build then produces the same IDE
// next month as it does now.
//
// `checksums` maps a release asset name to its SHA-256. Pinning a version
// without pinning the checksums still leaves the download unverified beyond
// HTTPS, so `build.sh --record` fills this in: run it once on a machine with
// network access and commit what it writes.
{
  "version": null,
  "checksums": {}
}
